  "description": "Purchasing a Stock and a Quick Portfolio Update",
  "body_html": "<p>We first traded this stock successfully in September 2025, for a modest profit. But that was never the BIG move I was targeting. The move stalled as October and November became a macro dead zone for the markets: higher for longer rates, heavy treasury issuance, and earnings uncertainty froze momentum across the market. While most names never recovered, this stock held bullish structure and just made a clean breakout from consolidation. <strong>I am buying it again</strong>.   </p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/subscribe?\"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p><p>Additionally, our <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$WSFS&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> position is now up over +20% profit. I am contemplating trimming <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$BFST&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> , which is up +7.2% at time of writing and adding to our winner. Double down on winners, trim or sell weakness. Seeing a few weak signs with BFST. Just giving you a heads up. I like to operate with foresight with you all. I will update the quick notes when and if I do this.</p><h4>This is a quick update, so the stock is: </h4>",
  "has_dynamic_content": false,
